%% DM26-0670

%% Phase 2 of the sandbox-local bootstrap: Flux reconciles the deployment repo, layer by layer.
%% This ran on a podman dev node on 2026-10-19, and from the dev pod on 2026-10-21 (registry and deployment git server in the cluster).
%% Read against infra/ on 2026-11-04. The layers, their order and what each waits for are declared in
%% infra/targets/T/target.nu (apply_layers) and travel in the repo as the Kustomizations under flux/.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Up as infra/flux.nu wait<br/>called by up.nu
    participant SC as Flux source-controller
    participant DGit as deployment git server<br/>(in the cluster, polar-deploy)
    participant KC as Flux kustomize-controller
    participant K as Kubernetes API
    participant Reg as registry in the cluster<br/>(nodes pull from localhost:30500)
    participant W as workloads of the layer

    Up->>DGit: git ls-remote as "flux": the commit that was published
    SC->>DGit: git clone over mTLS, presenting the "flux" certificate<br/>(Secret deploy-repo-auth), trusting ca.crt, by its Service, polar-deploy-git.polar-deploy.svc.cluster.local:9443
    DGit->>DGit: the identity "flux" is a reader of deploy-T: allowed
    DGit-->>SC: the tree at COMMIT (layers/, flux/, provenance.json, deployment-record.json, a README)
    SC->>K: artifact for COMMIT, GitRepository Ready

    Note over KC,W: each layer is a Kustomization that dependsOn the one before
    KC->>K: platform: namespaces, serviceaccounts, local-path-provisioner, storage-class<br/>(the namespaces were applied by up.nu, Flux adopts them)
    KC->>K: cert-issuer: PVC, ConfigMap, Service, Deployment
    K->>Reg: kubelet pulls the image (Always: it asks the registry for every container that starts)
    K->>W: cert-issuer starts using Secret cert-issuer-ca and ConfigMap polar-ca, both made in phase 1
    KC->>KC: health check: Deployment cert-issuer is ready, then the next layer

    KC->>K: data: neo4j, postgres, keycloak
    Note over KC,W: No health check on this layer. Neo4j's polar-init waits for the credentials agent,<br/>which is in a later layer that depends on this one: waiting here would never end.<br/>up.nu waits for Neo4j after every layer is applied.

    KC->>K: cassini: cassini-resources, cassini (a Deployment)
    KC->>KC: health check: Deployment cassini is ready.<br/>This is the gate: a client that starts first attaches to a broker that is about to go away

    KC->>K: identity: credentials-agent and credentials-agent-observer (Deployments)
    KC->>KC: health check: Deployments credentials-agent and credentials-agent-observer are ready

    KC->>K: agents: jaeger, ace, kube, jira, git, soft-state, polar-git-server, scheduler,<br/>oci-registry-resolver, attestation-agent (Deployments)
    Note over KC,W: This layer has no wait_for, so no health check. jira-observer with no Jira set up holds the problem<br/>and stays up (held_agent_and_dynamic_setting)

    Note over KC,W: as each workload's pod starts, polar-init gets a certificate carrying its declared topics and groups<br/>(p:pub, p:sub, g:, from the model the render wrote). The broker, cert-issuer and the credentials agent<br/>run on that floor before any policy exists, and every subscribe and publish is decided at the broker.<br/>(general/topic_floor_issuance)
    KC->>K: record each Kustomization Ready at COMMIT
    loop every 5 seconds until the timeout
        Up->>K: every Kustomization Ready, and applied from COMMIT (not an earlier commit)?
        alt a layer has been waiting 15 s on a health check begun under an older spec or revision
            Up->>KC: restart the kustomize-controller, at most three times<br/>(a reconcile finishes under the spec it began with, up to its 10 minute timeout)
        end
    end
    alt a layer is unhealthy at the timeout
        Up-->>Up: name the layers and Flux's<br/>message, exit non-zero
        Note over Up,KC: run the same command again: nothing is redone, it waits
    else all Ready
        Up-->>Up: phase 2 is done
    end

    Note over SC,K: Afterwards, with no one running anything: Flux checks the repo on an interval,<br/>applies a new commit, prunes what left the repo, and puts back what was edited in the cluster.<br/>A Deployment rolls (Recreate) when its pod template changes: a rebuilt image changes the digest it names,<br/>and a changed ConfigMap changes the polar.dev/config-hash fingerprint published with it.
